{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam configuration and documentation","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG",".bridge_state/projects.json","status","type","link","priority","create_defaults"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","mapping seam","provider-neutral","migration safety","backward compatibility","configuration reference"],"propositions":["The mapping seam configuration surface requires authoritative end-to-end documentation covering the reserved [tool.rebar.mapping] section, axis catalog, three-layer merge, per-project keying, and fail-closed validation.","The mapping seam must be documented as provider-neutral with a reuse contract enabling future integrations (Linear, GitLab, GitHub-Issues) independent of specific CI providers.","The feature must be documented as fully backward-compatible and additive: an absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior, and rollback is a delete operation with no store migration required.","All mapping behaviors must be covered by injected-transport unit tests with no live Jira dependency and no specific CI provider requirement."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787472000478170001,"uuid":"8b2f473a-9e22-4d43-ad92-59bd93fff398"}